From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:58:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(lefthook-wiring): cut cognitive complexity of
 resolveGitHooksDir + installNativeGitHooks

Address CodeRabbit/SonarCloud Major maintainability findings on the new module.
Behavior is unchanged (all lefthook-wiring behavioral tests still pass; native-fallback
e2e still installs sentinel hooks and verifies enforcement active).

- resolveGitHooksDir: extract the linked-worktree branch into resolveWorktreeHooksDir +
  resolveWorktreeCommonDir, so the top function is a flat dir/file/else dispatch.
- installNativeGitHooks: extract per-hook logic into writeNativeHook +
  shouldPreserveExistingHook + backupHookOnce; the loop is now a single call per hook.
- Add tests locking the symlink/directory security guard of forgeShouldWriteLefthookConfig
  (returns false for a symlinked or directory lefthook.yml).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
